{"id": "prd-tui-boot-splash-firstframe", "type": "screen", "surface": "tui", "area": "shell", "title": "Boot splash & first frame (nav menu)", "intent": "User launches `fulcrum tui` and sees TUI entry point with navigation menu", "sources": ["apps/tui/src/index.ts:365-389", "tests/tui/smoke.test.ts:85-203"], "acceptance": ["Fulcrum banner or title renders on first frame", "Status bar shows email and org ID at bottom (resolved from auth.whoami())", "Navigation menu lists: Projects, Tasks, Sprints, Docs, Planning, Memory, Runs, Repos, Artifacts, Search, Notifications, Rules, Skills, Routing, Inference, Doctor, Auth, Flags, Activity, Audit", "Cursor starts at index 0 (Projects)", "j/k or arrow keys move cursor, Enter opens screen, q exits entire TUI", "Status shows (unauthenticated) fallback if auth service unavailable"], "anti_patterns": ["Status bar shows stale or cached auth state", "Navigation menu appears before status bar renders", "First frame takes >200ms to render or blocks on external API", "No fallback when whoami() fails"], "interactions": [{"selector": "nav:full", "action": "nav", "expected": "TUI starts on nav menu, status bar visible"}, {"selector": "nav:cursor", "action": "key", "expected": "j moves cursor down, k moves up, >=0 and <items.length"}, {"selector": "nav:open", "action": "key", "expected": "Enter opens selected screen, nav menu disappears"}, {"selector": "nav:exit", "action": "key", "expected": "q exits TUI cleanly"}], "critique_focus": "Does nav menu render synchronously? Does status bar block? Is cursor navigation reliable?", "manual_simulation": "Run `fulcrum tui` in terminal. Expect: banner, status (email@org), menu items, j/k work, Enter opens, q quits.", "passes": false, "priority": "p0", "incentive": "entry point; no TUI without this", "status": "proposed", "op": "create", "agent": "seed-internal-tui", "ts": "2026-05-17T18:08:20.492762"}
{"id": "prd-tui-status-footer-connection-runtime", "type": "ui-element", "surface": "tui", "area": "shell", "title": "Status footer: API connection, runtime state, trace echo", "intent": "User sees at-a-glance health: auth state, org/email, agent runtime status, trace context", "sources": ["apps/tui/src/index.ts:498-550", "tests/tui/smoke.test.ts:100-127"], "acceptance": ["Footer line at bottom shows: `[email@org] | Trace: [trace-id] | Runtime: [status]`", "Status includes: org from auth.whoami(), email from auth.whoami()", "Inference health: shows 'green' if status=ok, 'yellow' if degraded, 'red' if down", "Trace ID visible if set (from context)", "Footer updates when status changes (polling or stream)", "If API disconnected: shows 'disconnected' hint, cursor can open reconnect dialog"], "anti_patterns": ["Status bar shows stale email after login", "Trace ID always blank even when context active", "Health status never changes (no polling or listener)", "Footer text truncated or misaligned on narrow terminals (<80 cols)"], "interactions": [{"selector": "footer:email", "action": "nav", "expected": "Shows current user email"}, {"selector": "footer:org", "action": "nav", "expected": "Shows current org ID"}, {"selector": "footer:trace", "action": "nav", "expected": "Shows trace ID if context active"}, {"selector": "footer:runtime", "action": "nav", "expected": "Shows agent runtime status color"}], "critique_focus": "Is footer real-time? Does trace ID match request context? Readable on 80 columns?", "manual_simulation": "Launch TUI, check footer. Look for email, org, trace ID. Change project or start run, watch trace update.", "passes": false, "priority": "p0", "incentive": "user needs confidence API is connected; trace enables debugging", "status": "proposed", "op": "create", "agent": "seed-internal-tui", "ts": "2026-05-17T18:08:20.492762"}
{"id": "prd-tui-nav-domain-screens-projects", "type": "screen", "surface": "tui", "area": "nav", "title": "Main nav entry: Projects list", "intent": "User navigates to Projects, sees list of available projects, can create/select/delete", "sources": ["apps/tui/src/screens/projects.ts", "apps/tui/src/index.ts:365-366"], "acceptance": ["Screen title: 'Projects'", "Renders project rows: name, slug, repo path, status (ok/error/dirty)", "Selected row highlighted (reverse video or cursor indicator)", "Keybindings: j/k navigate, Enter open, n create new, d delete (with confirm), y show YAML", "Empty state: 'No projects. Press [n] to create one.'", "Create flow: prompt for name, slug, local path, template selection"], "anti_patterns": ["Project rows show no status or health", "Delete key (d) applies immediately without confirmation", "Cursor not visible on selected row", "Creating project blocks indefinitely if API slow"], "interactions": [{"selector": "projects:list", "action": "nav", "expected": "Rows render with name, slug, path"}, {"selector": "projects:select", "action": "key", "expected": "j/k move cursor, Enter opens detail"}, {"selector": "projects:create", "action": "key", "expected": "n opens create form"}, {"selector": "projects:delete", "action": "key", "expected": "d shows confirm prompt, y/n answer"}], "critique_focus": "Can user quickly scan projects? Is status visible? Does create prompt make sense?", "manual_simulation": "From nav, press j until Projects, Enter. See list. Try j/k, n (create), d (delete with confirm).", "passes": false, "priority": "p0", "incentive": "primary nav entry; users spend time here", "status": "proposed", "op": "create", "agent": "seed-internal-tui", "ts": "2026-05-17T18:08:20.492762"}
{"id": "prd-tui-nav-domain-screens-tasks", "type": "screen", "surface": "tui", "area": "nav", "title": "Main nav entry: Task list with filters", "intent": "User navigates to Tasks, sees filterable list, can create/edit/bulk-move tasks", "sources": ["apps/tui/src/screens/task-list.ts", "apps/tui/src/index.ts:367"], "acceptance": ["Screen title: 'Tasks (Project: [name])'", "Renders task rows: title, status, assignee, priority, due date, link count, run count", "Selected row highlighted; detail pane on right (if space) shows task context", "Keybindings: j/k nav, Enter open detail, Space multi-select, V range-select, F filter, / search, B board view, R report, D delete, Q quit", "Filter overlay: status, assignee, priority, label, due-date", "Bulk actions: change status (B), assign, set priority, link doc (L)", "Empty state: 'No tasks matching filters. Press [/] to search or [n] to create.'", "Trace spine visible: task ID, project ID, linked runs/docs/artifacts"], "anti_patterns": ["Multi-select not visible (no checkbox or indicator)", "Filters reset on navigation away and back", "Task detail pane doesn't fit on 120-col terminal", "Bulk actions block UI while saving"], "interactions": [{"selector": "tasks:list", "action": "nav", "expected": "Rows show title, status, assignee, priority"}, {"selector": "tasks:select-one", "action": "key", "expected": "j/k move cursor, Enter opens detail"}, {"selector": "tasks:select-multi", "action": "key", "expected": "Space marks selected, V range-selects"}, {"selector": "tasks:filter", "action": "key", "expected": "F opens filter dialog, can filter by status/assignee/priority"}, {"selector": "tasks:search", "action": "key", "expected": "/ opens search input, filters results live"}, {"selector": "tasks:bulk-move", "action": "key", "expected": "B (bulk status), shows available statuses to apply"}], "critique_focus": "Is list responsive to filters? Can user see multi-select? Does detail pane add value or clutter?", "manual_simulation": "Nav to Tasks. See list. Try j/k, Space (multi-select), F (filter), / (search), B (bulk), Enter (detail).", "passes": false, "priority": "p0", "incentive": "core workflow; users spend 30% of time here", "status": "proposed", "op": "create", "agent": "seed-internal-tui", "ts": "2026-05-17T18:08:20.492762"}
{"id": "prd-tui-nav-domain-screens-planning", "type": "screen", "surface": "tui", "area": "nav", "title": "Main nav entry: Planning workflow (planning breakdown)", "intent": "User opens Planning, sees approved plan breakdown, can review/execute tasks, track workflow state", "sources": ["apps/tui/src/screens/planning-breakdown.ts", "apps/tui/src/index.ts:370"], "acceptance": ["Screen title: 'Planning'", "Displays approved-plan markdown breakdown as task tree", "Shows workflow state: planning \u2192 review \u2192 exec \u2192 QA \u2192 UAT", "Keybindings: j/k nav tasks, Enter detail, Space approve, G go-top, gg go-bottom, p preview context, r dispatch run, c create doc, m promote memory, a show approvals, e show errors, n show next steps", "Live run pane: shows in-flight agent session, transcript, tool timeline, artifacts, memory candidates", "Approval queue: pending decisions visible, prompt for approval before dispatch", "Context preview: task fields, docs, memory, repo slices, token estimate", "Trace: plan ID, approved-plan version, source doc refs, workflow config"], "anti_patterns": ["Approved plan is blank (no default fixture)", "Live run pane blocks keyboard input", "Approvals require modal popup instead of inline prompt", "Workflow state not visible (user doesn't know if in planning or exec)", "Memory candidates never surface"], "interactions": [{"selector": "planning:tree", "action": "nav", "expected": "Task tree renders with indent, status icons"}, {"selector": "planning:select", "action": "key", "expected": "j/k move, Enter opens detail with context"}, {"selector": "planning:preview", "action": "key", "expected": "p shows context bundle preview (docs, memory, repo slices)"}, {"selector": "planning:dispatch", "action": "key", "expected": "r opens routing decision, shows approvals if needed, dispatches run"}, {"selector": "planning:live-run", "action": "nav", "expected": "Right pane shows transcript, tool events, artifacts as run progresses"}, {"selector": "planning:state", "action": "nav", "expected": "Header shows workflow state: planning/review/exec/qa/uat"}], "critique_focus": "Can user understand workflow state at a glance? Is context preview intuitive? Do approvals feel natural?", "manual_simulation": "Nav to Planning. See tree. Try p (preview context), r (dispatch), watch live run appear on right. Try Space (approve decision).", "passes": false, "priority": "p0", "incentive": "human journey H4 (run agents); core value prop", "status": "proposed", "op": "create", "agent": "seed-internal-tui", "ts": "2026-05-17T18:08:20.492762"}
{"id": "prd-tui-nav-domain-screens-runs", "type": "screen", "surface": "tui", "area": "nav", "title": "Main nav entry: Agent runs supervision", "intent": "User navigates to Runs, sees running/queued/completed agent sessions, can supervise/cancel/approve", "sources": ["apps/tui/src/screens/runs.ts", "apps/tui/src/index.ts:372"], "acceptance": ["Screen title: 'Agent Runs'", "Renders run rows: task title, status (running/done/failed/blocked), agent, start time, duration, trace ID", "Selected run shows detail: context, transcript, tool events, diff, artifacts, memory candidates, approvals", "Keybindings: j/k nav, Enter detail, d cancel (with confirm), y show YAML, q quit", "Live updates: transcript cursor moves as agent writes, tool events appear, artifacts list grows", "Approval prompts: show decision point, context for decision, yes/no/skip", "Empty state: 'No runs yet. Go to a task and press [r] to start a run.'", "Trace: run ID, task ID, context bundle version, routing decision, attempt number"], "anti_patterns": ["Transcript frozen (doesn't scroll to latest message)", "Approval prompt requires modal navigation", "Run list not sorted by start time (newest first)", "Canceling run blocks UI while server processes"], "interactions": [{"selector": "runs:list", "action": "nav", "expected": "Rows show task, status, agent, start time, duration"}, {"selector": "runs:select", "action": "key", "expected": "j/k move, Enter opens detail"}, {"selector": "runs:detail-transcript", "action": "nav", "expected": "Transcript scrolls to show latest agent message"}, {"selector": "runs:detail-approvals", "action": "nav", "expected": "Approval prompt visible with context, yes/no options"}, {"selector": "runs:cancel", "action": "key", "expected": "d shows confirm, y cancels run"}, {"selector": "runs:live", "action": "nav", "expected": "If run active, transcript and artifacts update live"}], "critique_focus": "Can user supervise a running agent? Are approvals easy to grant? Does live transcript feel responsive?", "manual_simulation": "Nav to Runs. If empty, start a run from Tasks. Watch transcript appear live. Try approvals. Try d (cancel).", "passes": false, "priority": "p0", "incentive": "agent supervision is core interaction; users need confidence", "status": "proposed", "op": "create", "agent": "seed-internal-tui", "ts": "2026-05-17T18:08:20.492762"}
