{"id": "prd-tui-screen-keybindings-vim-style", "type": "feature", "surface": "tui", "area": "interaction", "title": "Screen keybindings (vim-style navigation)", "intent": "All list/table screens support j/k/gg/G/enter/esc/q navigation", "sources": ["apps/tui/src/screens/task-list.ts:keybindings", "apps/tui/src/screens/projects.ts:keybindings", "tests/tui/smoke.test.ts:244-273"], "acceptance": ["j = move cursor down (or \u2193)", "k = move cursor up (or \u2191)", "gg = jump to first item", "G = jump to last item", "/ = open search/filter input", "Enter = open selected item detail", "Esc = close overlay or return to parent screen", "q = quit screen (return to nav menu)", "Space = multi-select (on list screens)", "V = range-select (on list screens)", "Cursor never wraps (stays at 0 or max when hitting bounds)", "Visual feedback on selected row (reverse video or highlight color)"], "anti_patterns": ["j moves down but k doesn't move up (inconsistent)", "gg/G don't work (user has to mash j/k)", "Cursor wraps around (confusing)", "Selected row has no visual indicator"], "interactions": [{"selector": "list:nav-down", "action": "key", "expected": "j or \u2193 moves cursor down by 1"}, {"selector": "list:nav-up", "action": "key", "expected": "k or \u2191 moves cursor up by 1"}, {"selector": "list:jump-top", "action": "key", "expected": "gg jumps to first item"}, {"selector": "list:jump-bottom", "action": "key", "expected": "G jumps to last item"}, {"selector": "list:open", "action": "key", "expected": "Enter opens selected item"}, {"selector": "list:close", "action": "key", "expected": "Esc closes detail or q returns to nav"}, {"selector": "list:select", "action": "key", "expected": "Space toggles multi-select, V range-selects"}], "critique_focus": "Are vim keys intuitive? Is navigation responsive? Does multi-select feel natural?", "manual_simulation": "Nav to Tasks. Try j (down), k (up), gg (top), G (bottom), Space (select), V (range), / (filter).", "passes": false, "priority": "p0", "incentive": "power-user ergonomics; vim fans expect this", "status": "proposed", "op": "create", "agent": "seed-internal-tui", "ts": "2026-05-17T18:08:20.492762"}
{"id": "prd-tui-detail-pane-relationships", "type": "ui-element", "surface": "tui", "area": "layout", "title": "Detail pane: task/run/doc/artifact relationships", "intent": "When selected item has detail, right pane shows: linked docs, runs, artifacts, memory, comments, audit, trace spine", "sources": ["apps/tui/src/screens/task-detail.ts", "apps/tui/src/screens/runs.ts (run detail pane)", "09.6-HUMAN-WORKFLOW-UX-SPEC.md:98-105"], "acceptance": ["Detail pane width: min 50 cols, max 80 cols; if terminal <130 cols, hide pane and use Enter for detail screen", "Task detail pane shows: status, priority, assignee, project, parent, dependencies, cycle, due date, branch/path, run count, doc links, artifact count, memory count, audit count", "Run detail pane shows: task, context bundle version, route decision, live transcript, tool timeline, artifacts, memory candidates, approvals, diff", "Doc detail pane shows: project, path, author, created/edited, backlinks, linked tasks/runs/artifacts/memory, versions", "Each link is selectable (j/k move focus, Enter navigate)", "Trace visible: entity ID, project ID, linked parent IDs", "Pane updates live if subscription active (e.g., transcript cursor moves)"], "anti_patterns": ["Detail pane fixed width makes content wrap awkwardly", "Links not interactive (view-only, can't navigate)", "Pane doesn't update live (transcript frozen)", "Pane hides on narrow terminal without fallback"], "interactions": [{"selector": "detail:render", "action": "nav", "expected": "Pane appears on right side when item selected"}, {"selector": "detail:scroll", "action": "key", "expected": "j/k scroll within pane content"}, {"selector": "detail:navigate", "action": "key", "expected": "Enter on link navigates to linked entity"}, {"selector": "detail:live", "action": "nav", "expected": "If subscription active, transcript updates live"}], "critique_focus": "Does pane fit on typical terminals? Can user navigate links? Does live update feel responsive?", "manual_simulation": "Open a task. See detail pane on right (if terminal wide enough). Try j/k (scroll), Tab (focus links), Enter (navigate).", "passes": false, "priority": "p0", "incentive": "trace spine visibility; users need context without extra navigation", "status": "proposed", "op": "create", "agent": "seed-internal-tui", "ts": "2026-05-17T18:08:20.492762"}
{"id": "prd-tui-modal-confirmation-escape-trap", "type": "feature", "surface": "tui", "area": "interaction", "title": "Confirmation modal: delete/cancel/destructive actions", "intent": "Before destructive action, modal prompts user, Escape cancels, y/n answers", "sources": ["apps/tui/src/screens/projects.ts:delete-confirm", "apps/tui/src/screens/task-list.ts:delete-confirm"], "acceptance": ["Before delete/cancel: modal overlay appears with message, e.g., 'Delete project [name]? (y/n)'", "Modal blocks background input (can't navigate list behind modal)", "Keybindings: y = yes (confirm), n = no (cancel), Esc = cancel", "After answer, modal closes and returns focus to list", "Modal centered on screen, readable text, no timeout (waits for user input)", "Trace: shows action context (e.g., 'Delete project proj-1')"], "anti_patterns": ["Delete action applies immediately (no confirm)", "Modal doesn't trap Escape (user accidentally confirms)", "Modal times out and auto-confirms", "No visual distinction from background (modal not obvious)"], "interactions": [{"selector": "modal:show", "action": "key", "expected": "d (delete) on item shows confirmation modal"}, {"selector": "modal:confirm", "action": "key", "expected": "y confirms, action executes, modal closes"}, {"selector": "modal:cancel", "action": "key", "expected": "n or Esc cancels, modal closes, no action taken"}], "critique_focus": "Is modal obvious? Can user accidentally confirm? Does Escape always work?", "manual_simulation": "From task list, try d (delete). See modal. Press n or Esc (no action). Try y (action executes).", "passes": false, "priority": "p0", "incentive": "safety; prevents accidental deletes", "status": "proposed", "op": "create", "agent": "seed-internal-tui", "ts": "2026-05-17T18:08:20.492762"}
{"id": "prd-tui-status-footer-disconnected-reconnect", "type": "feature", "surface": "tui", "area": "shell", "title": "API disconnected state with reconnect hint", "intent": "If API becomes unavailable, footer shows 'disconnected', user can press r to reconnect", "sources": ["apps/tui/src/index.ts:status-management", "tests/tui/smoke.test.ts:149-168"], "acceptance": ["Normal state: footer shows 'ok'", "If API unreachable: footer changes to 'disconnected' (red color)", "Disconnected state persists: queued operations queue locally", "User can press r (global hotkey) to attempt reconnect", "If reconnect succeeds: footer returns to 'ok', queued ops flush", "If reconnect fails: footer stays 'disconnected', shows retry hint", "All screens remain navigable even while disconnected (read-only fallback mode)"], "anti_patterns": ["TUI freezes when API disconnects", "No visual indication of disconnect state", "User must restart TUI to reconnect", "Queued ops lost on reconnect failure"], "interactions": [{"selector": "disconnect:detect", "action": "nav", "expected": "Footer changes to 'disconnected' if API unreachable"}, {"selector": "disconnect:hint", "action": "nav", "expected": "Footer shows 'Press [r] to reconnect'"}, {"selector": "disconnect:reconnect", "action": "key", "expected": "r attempts to reconnect to API"}, {"selector": "disconnect:recovery", "action": "nav", "expected": "If reconnect succeeds, footer returns 'ok', queued ops flush"}], "critique_focus": "Can user recognize disconnect? Is reconnect intuitive? Do queued ops work?", "manual_simulation": "Disconnect API (stop server or unplug network). See 'disconnected' in footer. Press r. Reconnect server. Watch footer return to 'ok'.", "passes": false, "priority": "p1", "incentive": "resilience; users work in unstable networks", "status": "proposed", "op": "create", "agent": "seed-internal-tui", "ts": "2026-05-17T18:08:20.492762"}
