ortant items?", "Is mark-read action intuitive (click = nav, button = mark)?", "Does real-time badge update feel responsive?"], "manual_simulation": "1. Get mentioned in comment: @alice\n2. Verify bell badge shows '1'\n3. Click bell \u2192 notification appears: 'Alice mentioned you in Architecture doc'\n4. Click notification \u2192 navigate to doc + scroll to comment\n5. Verify notification marked as read (no longer bold)\n6. Click 'Mark all as read' \u2192 all notifications become faded\n7. View tabs: All, Comments (shows only comment notifs), Mentions", "passes": false, "priority": "p0", "incentive": "Notifications are primary discovery and response mechanism", "status": "proposed", "op": "create", "agent": "seed-docmost-search", "ts": "2026-05-17T15:09:45.148795"}
{"id": "prd-docmost-notifications-mention", "type": "feature", "surface": "web", "area": "notifications", "title": "Notifications: Comment Mention (@mention)", "intent": "Trigger notification when user is mentioned in comment via @mention, with link back to comment and unsubscribe option", "sources": ["apps/server/src/core/comment/comment.service.ts:queueCommentNotification", "apps/server/src/core/notification/notification.processor.ts"], "acceptance": {"trigger": ["User @mentioned in comment (any page in workspace member's spaces)", "Notification queued immediately after comment created", "Notification created only for mentioned user, not comment creator"], "content": ["Notification text: '@Alice mentioned you in [Page Title]: [snippet of comment]'", "Link target: page URL + anchor to comment", "Mention link in notification clickable and direct to exact comment"], "delivery": ["In-app notification: instant (WS event)", "Email notification: delayed 5 min, batched with other events (per user setting)", "Toast alert: on mention (dismissible)"], "criteria": ["Mention extraction from ProseMirror JSON works correctly", "Only active users (not deactivated) receive mention", "Per-user mention notification setting honored", "Unsubscribe link from email works"]}, "anti_patterns": ["\u274c Mention to non-members (permission error)", "\u274c Mention triggers multiple notifications for same comment", "\u274c No email delivery (users miss mentions)", "\u274c Email unsubscribe broken", "\u274c Mention to deleted/deactivated users"], "interactions": ["Type comment: 'Hi @alice, please review'", "@alice autocomplete shows (only space members)", "Select @alice \u2192 insert mention link", "Post comment \u2192 mention extracted + notification queued", "Alice receives in-app notification + email (if enabled)", "Click notification \u2192 navigate to page + focus comment", "Click 'Mute mentions from Alice' in email \u2192 user preference set"], "critique_focus": ["Does mention extraction work with multiple mentions?", "Are email batches delivered at reasonable time (not too delayed)?", "Can users customize per-comment-author muting?", "Is mention anchor (scroll target) accurate?"], "manual_simulation": "1. Alice and Bob in same space\n2. Bob comments: '@alice please check this'\n3. Alice receives in-app toast: '@Bob mentioned you in [page]'\n4. Bell badge shows '1'\n5. Alice checks email notification (5 min later)\n6. Click email link \u2192 navigate to page + scroll to Bob's comment\n7. Alice clicks 'Mute mentions in [space]' \u2192 future @mentions muted", "passes": false, "priority": "p0", "incentive": "Mentions drive direct collab and ensure visibility", "status": "proposed", "op": "create", "agent": "seed-docmost-search", "ts": "2026-05-17T15:09:45.148795"}
{"id": "prd-docmost-notifications-settings", "type": "feature", "surface": "web", "area": "notifications", "title": "Notifications: Settings (Per-Channel, Per-Category, Quiet Hours)", "intent": "Allow users to customize notification delivery: in-app vs email, mute categories, set quiet hours", "sources": ["apps/server/src/core/notification/notification.service.ts:queueEmail", "apps/server/src/core/notification/notification.constants.ts:NotificationTypeToSettingKey"], "acceptance": {"ui": ["Settings > Notifications page with sections:", "  \u2022 Delivery: Email toggle, In-app toggle, Quiet hours (time range)", "  \u2022 Categories: Mentions, Comments, Page updates, Subscriptions (checkbox each)", "  \u2022 Per-page rules: Mute [page name] or Watch [page] (from page context)", "  \u2022 Email digest: Daily/Weekly/Never (batch multiple notifications)"], "behavior": ["Per-user settings stored in DB user.settings.notifications", "Quiet hours: suppress email only (in-app still shows)", "Category muting affects both in-app and email", "Page-level mute overrides global setting (per-page granularity)", "Settings take effect immediately"], "criteria": ["Settings validated (time range 0-24, valid enum values)", "Default: email enabled, all categories on, no quiet hours", "Persist settings to user.settings JSON blob"]}, "anti_patterns": ["\u274c Email settings can't be disabled (user stuck)", "\u274c No per-page muting (must mute entire category)", "\u274c Quiet hours not respected (emails still sent)", "\u274c Settings take time to apply (confusion)", "\u274c No way to preview what quiet hours will do"], "interactions": ["Navigate to Settings > Notifications", "Toggle 'Email notifications' off \u2192 email never sent", "Toggle 'Comments' category \u2192 category emails disabled", "Set Quiet hours 22:00 - 08:00 \u2192 emails batched until 08:00", "Hover category \u2192 show 'Mute in [current page]' option", "Click mute \u2192 notification for this page type disabled (others still on)", "Save \u2192 confirmation toast 'Notification settings updated'"], "critique_focus": ["Are defaults reasonable (not too noisy)?", "Is per-page muting discoverable?", "Do quiet hours feel intuitive?", "Can users export/import notification rules?"], "manual_simulation": "1. Open Settings > Notifications\n2. Verify 'Email' on, 'In-app' on, 'Quiet hours' empty\n3. Toggle 'Email' off \u2192 no email notifications sent henceforth\n4. Set Quiet hours 22:00-08:00 \u2192 emails batch until 08:00\n5. Toggle 'Comments' category off \u2192 comment notifications stop\n6. Open Architecture doc \u2192 hover bell > 'Mute Architecture' \u2192 mutes only this page\n7. Verify other pages still trigger notifications\n8. Save \u2192 see 'Settings updated' confirmation", "passes": false, "priority": "p1", "incentive": "Notification fatigue is primary pain; customization essential", "status": "proposed", "op": "create", "agent": "seed-docmost-search", "ts": "2026-05-17T15:09:45.148795"}
{"id": "prd-docmost-notifications-page-subscription", "type": "feature", "surface": "web", "area": "notifications", "title": "Notifications: Page Subscription Rule + Watcher List", "intent": "Subscribe to page updates (notify on any edit) and view page watcher list with avatars; auto-add watchers on comment", "sources": ["apps/server/src/core/watcher/watcher.service.ts", "apps/server/src/core/notification/notification.service.ts"], "acceptance": {"ui": ["Page toolbar: 'Watch' button (bell icon) + watcher avatar stack", "Click Watch \u2192 toggle subscription status", "Click avatar stack \u2192 show watcher list (name + joined date)", "Watcher list shows current user starred/pinned", "Tooltip on Watch button: 'Watch to get notified of page edits'"], "behavior": ["Watch: POST /watchers { pageId, type: 'page' } \u2192 auto-subscribe to edits", "Unwatch: DELETE /watchers/{pageId}", "Auto-watch on comment: add commenter to page watchers (QueueJob.ADD_PAGE_WATCHERS)", "Page edit: emit notification to all watchers", "List watchers: GET /pages/{id}/watchers (paginated)"], "criteria": ["Watcher upsert prevents duplicates", "Auto-watch on comment doesn't create dups", "Watcher list shows avatars + names + joined date", "Notification only sent to space members (filter by permission)"]}, "anti_patterns": ["\u274c Watch button toggles but doesn't persist", "\u274c Watching page doesn't trigger notifications (false sense)", "\u274c Watcher list shows deleted users", "\u274c Unwatch doesn't stop notifications (still receiving)", "\u274c Non-space-members in watcher list"], "interactions": ["Click 'Watch' button \u2192 toggles to 'Watched' (filled bell)", "Hover avatar stack \u2192 tooltip with all watcher names", "Click avatar stack \u2192 drawer shows watcher list with join dates", "On comment: auto-add commenter to watchers (notification onscreen: '[You were added as watcher]')", "Edit page \u2192 watchers receive notification: '[User] edited [page]'"], "critique_focus": ["Is Watch affordance clear (vs Subscribe to notifications)?", "Does auto-watch on comment feel right (or annoying)?", "Can users easily see who's watching?", "Do page update notifications have right granularity (all edits vs major changes)?"], "manual_simulation": "1. Open Architecture doc\n2. Click Watch button (bell outline) \u2192 toggles to filled bell\n3. See avatar stack: you + Alice already watching\n4. Click avatars \u2192 drawer shows: You (just now), Alice (3 weeks ago), Bob (1 week ago)\n5. Add comment \u2192 onscreen note: 'You were added as watcher'\n6. Leave page\n7. Alice edits page \u2192 you receive notification: 'Alice edited Architecture'\n8. Click Watch again \u2192 unwatch \u2192 no more page edit notifs", "passes": false, "priority": "p1", "incentive": "Watchers drive organic follow-ups on important pages", "status": "proposed", "op": "create", "agent": "seed-docmost-search", "ts": "2026-05-17T15:09:45.148795"}
{"id": "prd-docmost-activity-page-feed", "type": "feature", "surface": "web", "area": "activity", "title": "Activity Feed: Per-Page Change Log", "intent": "Show detailed timeline of page changes (edits, comments, watchers added) with actor, action, target, timestamp, and undo capability", "sources": ["apps/server/src/core/session/session-activity.service.ts", "apps/server/src/database/migrations/20260213T085259-notifications.ts"], "acceptance": {"display": ["Activity sidebar/drawer (right side or tab in page view)", "Timeline format: avatar + actor name + action + target + timestamp", "Entry examples:", "  \u2022 'Alice edited [section name] 5 minutes ago'", "  \u2022 'Bob added comment on [selection] 1 hour ago'", "  \u2022 'You added Charlie as watcher 1 day ago'", "  \u2022 'System published page 2 days ago'", "Timestamps: relative (5 min ago) + tooltip with absolute (2026-05-17 14:32)"], "behavior": ["Fetch activity: GET /pages/{id}/activity (paginated, 20 per page)", "Filter by action type: all, edits, comments, watchers, published", "Show last 30 days by default, older via pagination", "Real-time: WS event adds new entry to top of feed"], "criteria": ["Activity logged for: page edit, comment creation/deletion, watcher add/remove, publish", "Not logged: view/open, sidebar toggle, search", "Timestamp accurate to event time (not log time)", "Actor always a real user (no system actors with unknown names)"]}, "anti_patterns": ["\u274c Activity log empty (no entries created)", "\u274c Timestamps off by hours (wrong timezone)", "\u274c Activity shows deleted users or inaccessible pages", "\u274c Real-time updates not present (stale after new action)", "\u274c No way to filter by action type (too much noise)"], "interactions": ["Open page \u2192 click Activity button (sidebar icon) \u2192 drawer slides open", "Timeline shows recent actions chronologically (newest first)", "Hover action entry \u2192 show 'Copy link' button (direct link to action)", "Hover action entry \u2192 show 'Undo' button (if applicable: edit/comment)", "Click actor avatar \u2192 show user profile", "Scroll down \u2192 load older activity"], "critique_focus": ["Is activity feed useful for tracking page evolution?", "Can users find specific changes easily (filter help)?", "Are timestamps consistent across timezones?", "Is undo clearly scoped (edit vs create)?"], "manual_simulation": "1. Open Architecture doc > Activity sidebar\n2. Verify timeline shows: 'Alice edited 5 min ago', 'Bob added comment 30 min ago', 'You added Charlie as watcher 1 hour ago'\n3. Hover action \u2192 'Undo' button visible (for edit/comment)\n4. Filter dropdown \u2192 select 'Edits only' \u2192 timeline filtered\n5. Scroll down \u2192 load older activity from last week\n6. WS event: Alice edits \u2192 new entry appears at top in real-time", "passes": false, "priority": "p1", "incentive": "Activity log is critical for audit, regression tracking, and understanding page history", "status": "proposed", "op": "create", "agent": "seed-docmost-search", "ts": "2026-05-17T15:09:45.148795"}
{"id": "prd-docmost-activity-workspace-feed", "type": "feature", "surface": "web", "area": "activity", "title": "Activity Feed: Workspace-Wide Activity Stream", "intent": "Show recent activity across entire workspace (all spaces + pages) for workspace overview, with filters by space/actor/action", "sources": ["apps/server/src/core/session/session-activity.service.ts", "apps/client/src/ee/ai/components/ai-search-result.tsx (similar structure)"], "acceptance": {"display": ["Portal > Activity tab (global view of workspace activity)", "Timeline: actor avatar + action + page/space name + timestamp", "Entries from all spaces user has access to", "Default: last 7 days, sortable by date (newest first) or by relevance"], "filters": ["Space filter: dropdown of spaces user can access", "Action type: edits, comments, watchers, publishes, all", "Actor filter: user multi-select to show only specific actors' activity", "Date range: last 7 days, 30 days, custom"], "behavior": ["Fetch: GET /workspace/activity { spaceIds, actions, actorIds, dateRange }", "Pagination: 50 per page, older via load-more button", "Real-time: WS event adds new entry from any space"], "criteria": ["Permission respected: only show activity from spaces user can access", "System actors filtered out (show real users only)", "Duplicates de-duped (same action not listed twice)", "Timestamps timezone-aware"]}, "anti_patterns": ["\u274c Activity from inaccessible spaces shown (privacy leak)", "\u274c No filtering (10K entries of noise)", "\u274c Only shows own activity (not collaborative view)", "\u274c Timestamps missing or incorrect", "\u274c Real-time updates not present"], "interactions": ["Navigate to Portfolio > Activity", "Timeline shows workspace-wide activity (all spaces)", "Apply filters: Space = 'Docs', Action = 'Comments' \u2192 results narrowed", "Actor filter: select 'Alice + Bob' \u2192 show only their activity", "Click activity entry \u2192 navigate to page + scroll to target", "Export activity (CSV) for audit purposes (optional)"], "critique_focus": ["Is workspace activity useful for workspace managers?", "Can filters prevent data overload?", "Is activity summary exportable for compliance?", "Do permissions correctly hide private spaces?"], "manual_simulation": "1. Navigate to Portfolio > Activity\n2. Verify last 7 days of workspace activity shown (all spaces)\n3. Entries: 'Alice edited Architecture', 'Bob commented in Runbook', 'Charlie added watcher to Team Handbook'\n4. Filter: Space = 'Docs' \u2192 shows only Docs space activity\n5. Filter: Action = 'Comments only' \u2192 shows only comments\n6. Filter: Actor = 'Alice' \u2192 shows only Alice's activity\n7. Click 'Architecture' entry \u2192 navigate to page + show edit\n8. Real-time: new action from Bob \u2192 appears at top instantly", "passes": false, "priority": "p2", "incentive": "Workspace activity enables transparency and collaboration oversight", "status": "proposed", "op": "create", "agent": "seed-docmost-search", "ts": "2026-05-17T15:09:45.148795"}
{"id": "prd-docmost-notifications-empty", "type": "feature", "surface": "web", "area": "notifications", "title": "Notifications Empty State", "intent": "Show helpful empty state when user has no notifications, with suggestions to participate or subscribe to pages", "sources": ["apps/server/src/core/notification/notification.service.ts:findByUserId (0 items)"], "acceptance": {"display": ["Large icon (\ud83d\udcec inbox) + heading 'All caught up!'", "Subtext: 'No new notifications. Check back later or subscribe to pages to stay updated.'", "Action buttons: 'Browse pages', 'Settings', 'Subscribe to a page'"], "behavior": ["Show when GET /notifications returns 0 items", "Browse pages: navigate to Portfolio > Pages (find pages to watch)", "Settings: open notification settings panel", "Subscribe: quick-open watch dialog for current page (if in page view)"]}, "anti_patterns": ["\u274c Blank white screen (no feedback)", "\u274c No action buttons (user stuck)", "\u274c Notification that 'You have no notifications' (redundant)"], "interactions": ["Open notifications \u2192 empty state shows", "Click 'Browse pages' \u2192 navigate to portfolio", "Click 'Settings' \u2192 open notification settings", "Click 'Subscribe to a page' \u2192 (if in page view) show quick watcher dialog"], "critique_focus": ["Is empty state encouraging (not discouraging)?", "Are action suggestions relevant?", "Does empty state match other empty states in app (consistency)?"], "manual_simulation": "1. Fresh user, no notifications yet\n2. Click bell icon \u2192 empty state: 'All caught up!'\n3. Verify action buttons visible\n4. Click 'Subscribe to a page' \u2192 watcher dialog (if in page view)", "passes": false, "priority": "p2", "incentive": "Empty state guidance prevents user confusion", "status": "proposed", "op": "create", "agent": "seed-docmost-search", "ts": "2026-05-17T15:09:45.148795"}
{"id": "prd-docmost-activity-empty", "type": "feature", "surface": "web", "area": "activity", "title": "Activity Feed Empty State", "intent": "Show helpful empty state when activity feed has no entries for selected filters", "sources": ["apps/server/src/core/session/session-activity.service.ts (0 items)"], "acceptance": {"display": ["Icon (\ud83d\udd0d) + 'No activity found'", "Subtext: 'Try adjusting filters or check another time period.'", "Filter reset button: 'Clear all filters'"], "behavior": ["Show when GET /activity returns 0 items", "Click 'Clear filters' \u2192 reset all filters to defaults, re-run search"]}, "anti_patterns": ["\u274c No empty state (looks broken)", "\u274c No way to reset filters", "\u274c Empty state doesn't suggest action"], "interactions": ["Apply filters (e.g., space + actor combo) \u2192 0 results", "Empty state: 'No activity found'", "Click 'Clear filters' \u2192 filters reset, activity shows"], "critique_focus": ["Is empty state message clear?", "Is filter reset easy to find?"], "manual_simulation": "1. Navigate to Activity\n2. Filter: Space = 'Archived' + Action = 'Comments' \u2192 0 results\n3. Empty state shows with 'Clear filters' button\n4. Click button \u2192 filters reset, activity appears", "passes": false, "priority": "p2", "incentive": "Empty state prevents user frustration with unexplained lack of results", "status": "proposed", "op": "create", "agent": "seed-docmost-search", "ts": "2026-05-17T15:09:45.148795"}
